---
const features = [
  [
    "01",
    "Trace the losing values",
    "The winning value is only half the story. Keep the definitions it replaced, with file and line provenance.",
    "Inspect a contribution",
    "project-model · $PROJECT/.claude/settings.json:2:12 · replaced_by_later_layer",
  ],
  [
    "02",
    "Precedence, not folklore",
    "Client-specific rules, not one universal merge. This demo focuses on the verified scalar /model subset.",
    "Compare the file orders",
    "Claude: user < shared < local. OpenCode: global < ancestor < nested (within the explicit project boundary).",
  ],
  [
    "03",
    "Reports with receipts",
    "Text for the terminal. Structured JSON for a report. Coverage gaps travel with the conclusion.",
    "Inspect report fields",
    "pointer: /model · status: partial · support: fixture_verified · effective_value: omitted",
  ],
  [
    "04",
    "Redact by default",
    "Protected values use a public projection. Unknown free text is not automatically safe to print.",
    "See the privacy example",
    "Only allowlisted values are reportable. Inspect the captured protected-value projection in the privacy section below.",
  ],
  [
    "05",
    "Changes without guesswork",
    "Compare compatible snapshots by value, provenance, and coverage. Two masks never prove equality.",
    "Inspect a protected comparison",
    "Protected values: comparison = unknown_redacted. Snapshots write only to explicitly requested output paths.",
  ],
  [
    "06",
    "A small tool, not an agent",
    "A local Rust CLI. No model calls, sockets, hooks, plugins, or client subprocesses at runtime.",
    "See a first command",
    "configlens explain /model --client claude --client-version 2.1.296",
  ],
];
---

<section id="features" class="section wrap">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">03 / LESS MYSTERY. MORE EVIDENCE.</p><h2>
        Find the file.<br />Understand the result.
      </h2>
    </div><p>
      A focused diagnostic tool.<br />Not a configuration manager. Not a
      security certification.
    </p>
  </div><div class="feature-grid">
    {
      features.map(([n, title, description, action, detail]) => (
        <article class="feature">
          <>
            <span class="feature-index mono">{n} /</span>
            <h3>{title}</h3>
            <p>{description}</p>
            <details>
              <>
                <summary>
                  {action} <span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                </summary>
                <p class="feature-detail">{detail}</p>
              </>
            </details>
          </>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</section>
